WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.990
The Namib Sand Sea, on
Africa's Atlantic coast:

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:09.610
a World Heritage Site
of 3,077,700 hectares.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.570
Its dunes reach 60 to 240 metres.

4
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.270
Then, at the Kuiseb
River, the sand sea stops.

5
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.790
North of it: gravel plains.

6
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.510
Rivers here normally flow for no more
than a few days in several years.

7
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.990
So how can a nearly dry river
stop a sea of giant dunes?

8
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.810
Is its channel too deep?

9
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.430
Have the dunes stopped?

10
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.110
In this mission, you'll explain how
a cold current shapes the climate,

11
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.450
and where the sand comes from.

12
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.550
Then you'll link dunes, rivers and
plains into one landscape system.

13
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.240
Your mission: explain how a river that
rarely flows can stop a sea of dunes.
